  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 DRC Emergency Appeal Population Movement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It covers the humanitarian response led by the DRC Red Cross, supported by IFRC, ICRC, and partner National Societies. The operation targets 500,000 people affected by armed conflict and displacement in North Kivu, South Kivu, and Ituri, with a budget of CHF 30 million</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The IFRC supports the DRC Red Cross through:
Integrated humanitarian response: health, WASH, livelihoods, and PGI activities.
Coordination mechanisms: Movement Coordination Agreement, L3 response, and joint missions (IFRC-ICRC-DRC RC).
Community engagement: 374,000 people reached via feedback systems.
Volunteer mobilization: 351 trained and insured volunteers.
Funding &amp; logistics: CHF 750,000 DREF loan and technical deployments (health, PGI, security, finance).
Despite insecurity and underfunding, operations have reached nearly 500,000 people with vital assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The appeal was launched in response to a massive humanitarian crisis caused by the escalation of the M23 conflict, leading to over 5.2 million internally displaced persons. Widespread violence, looting, and infrastructure destruction have triggered acute food insecurity, cholera outbreaks, and protection risks, particularly for women and children. The appeal seeks to reduce suffering, restore dignity, and meet urgent basic needs such as food, health, water, and protection.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation takes place mainly in the eastern provinces of the Democratic Republic of Congo: North Kivu, South Kivu, and Ituri, which are the epicentres of displacement and violence. Activities are concentrated in areas such as Goma, Lubero, Masisi, Rutshuru, Minova, Kalehe, and Uvira. Additional assistance extends to Rwanda, Burundi, and the Republic of Congo, which are receiving Congolese refugees. Coordination and logistics are handled from Kinshasa by the IFRC Country Cluster Delegation, with regional support from the IFRC Africa Regional Office in Nairobi.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation targets displaced families, host communities, women, and children under five, as well as survivors of sexual violence. Beneficiaries receive support in health, WASH, food, protection, and psychosocial care. Partners include the DRC Red Cross, IFRC, ICRC, ECHO, USAID/BHA, and regional Red Cross societies (Rwanda, Burundi, Congo-Brazzaville).</narrative>
  </description>
